The Book of the Dead and the Amulet of Yendor both curse your stuff. 
Ditch the Book after you've used it, and put your bags of holding into
a sack (see my earlier post on my ascension).  To avoid getting
teleported down levels with the Amulet, you must be chaotic; a helm of
opposite alignment is thus very handy for non-chaotic characters to
have before you get to Gehennom (I was lucky enough to find a blessed
+2 one much earlier in the game).  Don't forget to take it off after
you leave Gehennom, so you can wear something more useful (like a helm
of brilliance or telepathy) and sacrifice/pray to the correct god.

I kept a few scrolls of remove curse around for when the Amulet cursed
important stuff that I didn't keep in sacks.  But be careful when
reading a blessed scroll in case you want something in your inventory
to remain cursed (I had a cursed unicorn horn to confuse myself with to
read scrolls of gold detection and find portals in the endgame.  I have
since realized that this method is not the most efficient for producing
confusion, as a lot of other nasty things can happen to you before you
get the desired effect, so make sure to have a blessed horn too if you
use this option.  But I digress.).

I don't think the named weapons give you any point bonuses at the end,
but amulets of life saving (and possibly other amulets, at least the
wizard quest item) do.  I had 5 named weapons when I ascended and I
didn't see them listed in the list at the end of how many points the
gems and amulets were worth.

